          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em axion
            is a hypothetical type of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particle"} fundamental particle
            originally hypothesized (
            %a{:href => "#Weinberg77"}> Weinberg 77
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Wilczek78"} Wilczek 78
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+CP+problem"} strong CP problem
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            (see
            %a{:href => "#Wilczek78"} Wilczek 78
            for the early history) a variant model was found (
            %a{:href => "#DineFischlerSrednicki81"}> Dine-Fischler-Srednicki 81
            ), called the “invisible axion”, which does not violate experimental bounds.
          %p
            The “invisible axion” turns out to also be a natural candidate for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+matter"} dark matter
            (
            %a{:href => "#PreskillWiseWilczek83"}> Preskill-Wise-Wilczek 83
            ), hence potentially also solves one of the problems with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} standard model of cosmology
          %p
            More recently it is argued in
            %a{:href => "#HOTW16"} Hui-Ostriker-Tremaine-Witten 16
            that indeed axionic dark matter (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+dark+matter"}> fuzzy dark matter
            ) potentially solves the remaining problems of standard WIMP dark matter models: WIMP dark matter models work exceedingly well on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmological
            scales but has some experimental problems on the scale of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/galaxies"} galaxies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Broglie+wavelength"} de Broglie wavelength
            may be of the scale of galaxies and hence their quantum properties may become relevant at this scale to deviate in the right way from the WIMP models.
          %p
            The Pecchei-Quinn shift symmetry of the axion and the peculiar nature of the axion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction+term"} interaction term
            which are needed to make the axion model work this way have been argued to naturally arise in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-reduction"} KK-reduction
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AsArisingFromStringTheory"} below
          %h2#AsASolutionToTheStrongCPProblem As a solution to the strong CP problem
          %p
            The problem here is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"}> Yang-Mills theory
            ) a priori contains an arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+angle"} theta angle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ↦
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo +
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi θ
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\nabla \mapsto
                  \\frac{1}{g^2 }\int_X tr(F_\nabla \wedge \star F_\nabla)  \;+\;
                  \\theta \int_X tr(F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla)
          %p
            but that – since the term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tr(F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla)
            causes parity violation, which is strongly constrained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            – there must be some reason why
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            vanishes or else is extremely small.
          %p
            (Here the term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tr(F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Chern+class"} second Chern class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton+number"} instanton number
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
          %p
            The solution to this problem via axions is to assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            is not really a fundamental parameter, but instead is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+expectation+value"} vacuum expectation value
            of a dynamical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            (the axion).
          %p
            The idea is that a standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinetic+action"} kinetic action
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi kin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∝
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo *
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{kin} (a) \;\propto\; \int_X a \wedge \ast a
          %p
            together with the axion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            term
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi int
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∝
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mi a
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{int} (a,\nabla) \;\propto\;  \int_X a \, tr(F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla)
          %p
            makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            have vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+value"} expectation value
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle a\rangle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+angle"} theta angle
            with this expectation value
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta \coloneqq \langle a\rangle
          %p the theta angle vanishes.
          %h3#VafaWittenMechanism The Vafa-Witten mechanism
          %p
            That this is indeed the case is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#VafaWitten84"} Vafa-Witten 84, around (2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"} Wick rotated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            as follows:
          %p
            Under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"} Wick rotation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            pick up an imaginary factor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            expression for the Wick rotated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+energy"} vacuum energy
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mi vac
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi log
                          %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} (
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %munder
                              %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∇
                                %mo ,
                                %mi a
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo ∇
                            %mo ,
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi D
                            %mo ∇
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi D
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi log
                          %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} (
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %munder
                              %mo ∫
                              %mo ∇
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi g
                                  %mn 2
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∫
                                  %mi X
                              %mi tr
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi F
                                %mo ∇
                              %mo ∧
                              %mo ⋆
                              %msub
                                %mi F
                                %mo ∇
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi D
                              %mo ∇
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %munder
                                  %mo ∫
                                  %mi a
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                                %mi a
                                %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mo ∫
                                      %mi X
                                  %mi tr
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo ∇
                                  %mo ∧
                                  %msub
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo ∇
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mi D
                                  %mi a
                                  %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  E_{vac}(a)
                  \&amp;=
                  \- log \bigg(
                  \\textstyle{\underset{\nabla,a}{\int}}
                  \\exp\big(
                  \- S(\nabla,a)
                  \\big) \, D \nabla \, D a
                  \\bigg)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;=
                  \- log
                  \\bigg(
                  \\textstyle{\underset{\nabla}{\int}}
                  \\exp\big(
                  \\frac{1}{g^2 }
                  \\textstyle{\int_X}
                  tr(F_\nabla \wedge \star F_\nabla)
                  \\big)
                  \\, D \nabla
                  \\;
                  \\textstyle{\underset{a}{\int}}
                  \\exp\big(
                  \\mathrm{i} a \textstyle{\int_X}
                  tr(F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla)
                  \\big)
                  \\, D a
                  \\bigg)
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+unit"} imaginary unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{i}
            in front of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            in this expression, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"} real part
            of the argument of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithm"} logarithm
            necessarily becomes
            %em smaller
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %em larger
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi vac
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{vac}(a)
            must have a minimum at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta = 0
            (according to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#VafaWitten84"} Vafa-Witten 84, p.2
          %h2#AsArisingFromStringTheory In string theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            axion fields
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                are naturally present as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-reduction"} KK-reduction
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
                (e.g.
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "#SvrcekWitten06"} Svrcek-Witten 06
              %p reviewed below in:
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#AxionsAsKKReductionOfHigherGaugeFields"} As KK-Reduction of higher gauge fields
            %li
              %p
                are generically of positive but tiny mass (
                %a{:href => "#ADDKM09"}> ADDKM 09
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#AcharyaBobkovKumar10"} Acharya-Bobkov-Kumar 10
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+CP+problem"} strong CP problem
                and be candidates for
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+dark+matter"} BEC/superfluid/fuzzy dark matter
              %p reviewed below in:
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#StringyAxionPhenomenology"} Stringy axion phenomenology
          %p This makes axion fields in string theory form a curious confluence point relating
          %ul
            %li
              abstract concepts related to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
          %p with
          %ul
            %li
              fundamental question in
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} particle physics
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} cosmology
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mtext higher gauge theory
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mtext particle physics/cosmology phenomenology
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mtable
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mtext higher gauge fields
                                %mtr
